  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Calzone di scarola is a stuffed pizza. Two sheets of dough are rolled out, filled with braised escarole, sealed, and baked. The filling is Neapolitan: bitter escarole braised until soft with anchovies, olives, capers, raisins, and pine nuts. This is the classic sweet-and-sour pantry mix. The filling must be dry before it goes in. Wet filling steams rather than bakes and makes the base soft."
          }
        ]
      },
